.SS "setLiveAttributes (\fBAttributes\fP attrs)"

.PP
Associate an element with a live \fBAttributes\fP or \fBAnimatedAttributes\fP source\&. Rendering, bounds queries and hit tests read the source's current values\&. Multiple elements may share one source\&. Geometry and control points remain unchanged\&. The association follows the element when it is reordered; removed references never retarget a different element\&. Calling \fBsetAttributes()\fP replaces the association with a copy\&. \fBclearLiveAttributes()\fP freezes its current sample\&.

.PP
The association retains its final values and image/font resources if the source is destroyed or garbage collected\&. It does not retain or run the source's animation schedule\&. Advance a standalone \fBAnimatedAttributes\fP with animate(deltaSeconds), once per update regardless of how many elements share it or how often they are drawn\&. Keep a reference to the source while you intend to edit or advance it\&.

.PP
\fBDrawing\fP snapshots serialize current values, not the association or its schedule\&. \fBgetAttributes()\fP continues to return an independent value snapshot\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIattrs\fP Source whose values the element should follow\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Nothing\&. A removed element ignores this call\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const drawing = pdg\&.createDrawing();
const style = new pdg\&.AnimatedAttributes()\&.fillColor(new pdg\&.Color(1, 0, 0));
const element = drawing\&.addRect(new pdg\&.Rect(0, 0, 40, 40), style);
element\&.setLiveAttributes(style);
style\&.moveTo(100, 0, 1, pdg\&.linearTween);
// In your update callback, advance style\&.animate(deltaSeconds) once\&.
// Every subsequent draw uses the current sample automatically\&.

.fi
